// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/deploy-to-cloudflare-pages.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeDeployToCloudflarePages(path: "/recipes/deploy-to-cloudflare-pages", title: "Deploy to Cloudflare Pages — Recipes", description: "Deploy a WebFluent site to Cloudflare Pages: the build command and output folder to set, and a fallback for a single-page build.") {
    RecipeShell("Deploy to Cloudflare Pages", summary: "This recipe has Cloudflare Pages build a WebFluent site on every push and serve it, with the security headers the build writes.  You need a Cloudflare account and a Pages project connected to the repository; the build command installs `wf` as [Install wf on a build machine](/recipes/install-wf-in-ci) shows.  In the Pages project's build settings, set the build command:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "check-it", label: "Check it")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Install wf on a build machine", to: "/recipes/install-wf-in-ci"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Use environment values, and keep secrets out", to: "/recipes/environments-and-secrets"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to GitHub Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-github-pages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/deploy-to-cloudflare-pages.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            Terminal(lines: [
                        Line(command: "curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent/master/install.sh | WF_VERSION=v6.1.0 bash && ~/.webfluent/bin/wf build")
                    ])
            Markdown("and set the build output directory to `build`.\n\nFor a single-page build, also add `public/_redirects` with this line:")
            CodeBlock(#"/*  /index.html  200"#, title: "text")
        }
        Markdown("1. The build command installs `wf` and builds the site, the same command [Deploy to Netlify](/recipes/deploy-to-netlify) uses. Cloudflare Pages serves the `build` folder.\n2. The build copies `public/_redirects` to the root of `build/`. Its line answers every path with `index.html`, so a reload on a deep link reaches the single-page build's router.\n3. Cloudflare Pages reads `_headers` and `_redirects` the same way Netlify does, so the security headers apply with no further setting.")

        Heading("Check it", id: "check-it").h2

        Markdown("Check the response headers in the browser's network panel, as for Netlify, and open a deep link directly. Then go through [Check a deploy](/recipes/check-a-deploy).")

    }
}
